      "body": "Lab 2 §4.2 update (T2, executed): the D5 addressing contest is complete. Fixed H4/600-cell and E8-root codebooks, k-means, sign and recent/oracle arms at s ∈ {4,8,16,32} over the comparison tail, its ≥32-token long-range slice, and the five distractor rows. **NOT QUALIFIED**: h4-rht recall@1 0.9696 vs k-means-120 0.9813 at s=16 (outside 1 pt), decode not cheaper; NLL within 0.005 nats. Retired for serving at T=256/these bit rates; the remaining blocker is learnable relational ranking (the entity is admitted at dense q·k rank 1 but the dense reader ranks a more recent distractor above it), not admission. Full result `docs/integration/addressing-contest-result-2026-09-28.md` (draft PR References #973/#820).",
